    "solution": "Make a short hop in the low western throat, then dash left into the portal while airborne. The outlet turns the remaining dash upward through the floor your dash removed. Let the rise finish: the down-arrow crystal rejects the ascent and restores the dash on the fall. Dash right after that recovery to restore the phase bridge under you. Touch its visible tally: this opens the gun feed below, but the bridge now blocks the shot. Jump and dash off the bridge onto the broad eastern bank. Removing your old landing lets the converted portal shot reach the sealed receiver and open the last door; walk out when it retracts.",
    "nearestExisting": "F47 also restores an aerial phase landing; F13 spends a useful surface to open a later optical route. This room combines a direction-sensitive falling recovery with an opposing second use of that exact phase bridge: it must first catch the knight, then disappear as a projectile shutter. The bridge tally physically opens the shot feed only after arrival, so simply leaving the bridge absent cannot solve both jobs.",
    "novelty": "Recovering on the fall and restoring the bridge is only the arrival problem. The same portal subsequently carries a shot, and the useful landing has become the last obstruction in its path. The correct second use of the bridge is to leave it behind while withdrawing it; the final bank is safe while the shot completes its route.",
